{"l":5994,"g":7,"b":1,"cefr":"B1","role":"challenge","insight":"reframing","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'godt køb' på engelsk i 'This jacket was a real ___'?","o":["mistake","bargain","burden","surprise"],"a":"bargain","r":"'Bargain' = et godt køb."},
{"l":6001,"g":7,"b":2,"cefr":"B1","role":"challenge","insight":"reframing","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'Can you ___ the table for dinner, please?'","o":["put","do","lay","take"],"a":"lay","r":"Man siger 'lay the table' = dække bord. 'Put the table' betyder at stille bordet."},
{"l":6001,"g":7,"b":2,"cefr":"B1","role":"challenge","insight":"reframing","k":"l","variant":"authored","q":"Læs: 'The museum is free on Sundays, so it is always crowded. We went on a Tuesday instead and paid for our tickets.' Hvorfor tog de på museum en tirsdag?","o":["Fordi det var gratis","Fordi museet var lukket søndag","Fordi de havde fri fra skole","For at undgå mange mennesker"],"a":"For at undgå mange mennesker","r":"Om søndagen er der mange mennesker ('crowded'), så de valgte en anden dag."},
