{"l":6126,"g":7,"b":2,"cefr":"B1","role":"challenge","insight":"reframing","k":"h","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad siger man på engelsk, når du vil sige, at det er lige meget for dig, hvilken film jeres familie ser?","o":["I don't care of it.","It's all equal for me.","I don't mind which one.","I'm not minding."],"a":"I don't mind which one.","r":"'I don't mind' betyder, at det er lige meget for en. 'It's all equal' er en fordanskning."},
{"l":6167,"g":7,"b":2,"cefr":"B1","role":"challenge","insight":"reframing","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad betyder 'mark' i 'I got a good mark in my English test.'?","o":["mark","mærke","plet","karakter"],"a":"karakter","r":"'Mark' betyder her karakter. Falsk ven: en mark hedder 'field'."},
{"l":6182,"g":7,"b":2,"cefr":"B1","role":"challenge","insight":"reframing","k":"l","variant":"authored","q":"Læs: 'Oliver's phone battery died halfway through the trip, so he couldn't use the map. It took him two hours to find the hostel.' Hvorfor brugte Oliver så lang tid?","o":["Han kunne ikke se kortet","Han gik en omvej med vilje","Vandrerhjemmet var lukket","Han ventede på en bus"],"a":"Han kunne ikke se kortet","r":"Telefonen løb tør for strøm, så han kunne ikke bruge kortet."},
